From c91783cac54a602382309bb284a738052afc82ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exeroom536 <352890649+exeroom536@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:53:41 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/62] monitor: hand over a stopped array the manager replaces
 only once

If md stops an array while the manager replaces it (a spare added, a
device removed), the monitor holds it twice: deactivated - read_and_act()
has cleared ->container - and as ->replaces of the copy the manager put
in front of it.  wait_and_act() hands it to the manager both ways: as
stopped, then, once the manager has freed it, as replaced.  discard_this
is then the freed array - free(): double free in remove_old() - or
whatever malloc() has put at that address since: a live array, freed
under the monitor.  The copy meanwhile goes on with the descriptors
free_aa() closed for the stopped original, and closes them again.

manage_member() looks at a->container after the wait for the metadata
update of a spare ("managemon: no spare for an array md stopped while it
was being added"), but the monitor takes the update and sees the array
stopped in the same pass, and clears ->container only after it has
written the metadata.  The manager replaces the array meanwhile.

Leave a stopped array the manager is replacing (pending_discard) to the
pass that hands over the replaced one.  There, if md stopped it, the copy
is stopped too and takes its descriptors: the original gets ->container
back, so that free_aa() leaves them to the copy, which closes them when
it goes in turn.

A debug hook that stops the volume as soon as the manager has handed the
spare's update to the monitor (RAID1 on loop devices, a spare, --fail):
AMD - mdmon aborts (double free) 3 of 3; with the metadata write 60 ms
slower it lives, but closes 10 descriptors twice, 3 of 3.  IMSM - 6 of 6
the manager frees the live array that has the address of the freed one.
With this, 12 of 12: no abort, no descriptor closed twice, every array
handed over once.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5, an AI model by Anthropic.
---
 monitor.c | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/monitor.c b/monitor.c
index 7c4e4916..01e25c3b 100644
--- a/monitor.c
+++ b/monitor.c
@@ -756,10 +756,12 @@ static int wait_and_act(struct supertype *container, int nowait)
 	for (ap = aap ; *ap ;) {
 		a = *ap;
 		/* once an array has been deactivated we want to
-		 * ask the manager to discard it.
+		 * ask the manager to discard it - unless the manager
+		 * is replacing it: then it goes as the replaced array,
+		 * below, or the manager frees it twice.
 		 */
 		if (!a->container || a->to_remove) {
-			if (discard_this) {
+			if (discard_this || a == pending_discard) {
 				ap = &(*ap)->next;
 				continue;
 			}
@@ -875,8 +877,17 @@ static int wait_and_act(struct supertype *container, int nowait)
 			for (ap = &a->next; *ap && *ap != a->replaces;
 			     ap = & (*ap)->next)
 				;
-			if (*ap)
+			if (*ap) {
 				*ap = (*ap)->next;
+				if (!a->replaces->container) {
+					/* md stopped it meanwhile: so is the
+					 * copy, which closes the descriptors
+					 * they share (free_aa())
+					 */
+					a->replaces->container = container;
+					a->container = NULL;
+				}
+			}
 			discard_this = a->replaces;
 			a->replaces = NULL;
 			/* FIXME check if device->state_fd need to be cleared?*/
